  "title": "Thirtieth of May",
  "summary": "Iain explains: in January, before he knew Ruth, he applied to transfer to Dunedin to help his daughter with her twins. It came through a week ago and he hadn't found the words. For Ruth it echoes her ex-husband's three weeks' notice, but Sam points out this is the opposite of his dad. Ruth refuses long distance and asks for the six weeks, eyes open. Fiona writes to her kindly. Iain leaves on 29 May. The next morning Ruth plays the nocturne before 8.",
  "status": "final",
  "cliffhanger": null,
